OL,2,S]T$j5j5j5j=wj=j5j5D EUROPEAN CUP
OL,3,S]T/ +.!+.!*%*-'*%/*-*-(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,4,F
OL,5,FA goal by Ian Rush gaveCLiverpoolFa
OL,6,Fslender 1-0 lead to take to Portugal.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FLiverpool's top marksman finally beat
OL,9,FtheCBenficaFkeeper in the 66th minute.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FThe Welsh striker finished off a fine
OL,12,Ffour-man move with a strong header at
OL,13,Fthe far post after Johnston, Whelan and
OL,14,FKennedy had made the opening.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FSouness nearly added a second for
OL,17,FLiverpool when he ended a solo run with
OL,18,Fa shot of such power that Bento could
OL,19,Fonly parry it.
OL,20,F
OL,21,FBut the Benfica keeper managed to catch
OL,22,Fthe ball which shot into the air at the
OL,23,Fsecond attempt.
